serde_json's "indexmap" feature only changes its INTERNAL Map implementation — it does NOT implement Serialize for `indexmap::IndexMap` generally. So `json!(attrs)` with attrs: IndexMap<String, Vec<Row>> doesn't work. Fix: convert manually to serde_json::Map (which preserves order via preserve_order):

```rust
let attrs_value = Value::Object(attrs.into_iter().map(|(k, v)| (k, Value::Array(v.into_iter().map(Value::Object).collect()))).collect());
```
Or simpler — since sprite_attr_values returns IndexMap<String, Vec<Row>>, convert:
```rust
fn attrs_to_value(attrs: IndexMap<String, Vec<Row>>) -> Value {
    let mut m = Map::new();
    for (k, rows) in attrs {
        m.insert(k, Value::Array(rows.into_iter().map(Value::Object).collect()));
    }
    Value::Object(m)
}
```

